1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:10,512
In 1976, a school bus full of children vanished on a quiet country road. What happened next is one of the most incredible escapes ever.

2
00:00:10,862 --> 00:00:12,629
This is the Chowchilla kidnapping.

3
00:00:13,329 --> 00:00:23,160
Chowchilla, California. July 15th, 1976. Bus driver Ed Ray is taking twenty six children home from summer school.

4
00:00:23,510 --> 00:00:28,740
A van blocks the road. Three masked men force everyone off the bus at gunpoint.

5
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:34,895
The children and Ed are driven for hours, to a rock quarry about a hundred miles away.

6
00:00:35,245 --> 00:00:44,970
There, they're ordered down into a moving truck trailer that's been buried underground. The kidnappers plan to demand a ransom of five million dollars.

7
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:51,849
In the dark, the kids are scared. Ed keeps them calm, and the older children look after the little ones.

8
00:00:52,199 --> 00:01:00,283
After hours underground, Ed and fourteen year old Michael Marshall stack mattresses, pry at the roof, and start to dig.

9
00:01:00,633 --> 00:01:08,405
Finally, they break through. One by one, all twenty six children climb out into the night. Every single one survived.

10
00:01:09,105 --> 00:01:16,305
The three kidnappers were caught within weeks and sentenced to life in prison. Decades later, all three were paroled.

11
00:01:16,655 --> 00:01:23,717
A bus driver and a fourteen year old boy, who refused to give up. Follow for more true crime, animated.
